   "measured_at": "mujoco 3.12.0 / ogbench 1.2.1 reference; 224 px, camera front_pixels, 8 independent draws of 64 states from the env's own pool (reset + 0-25 random actions) on an RTX 3090 under MUJOCO_GL=egl, against swm's own render(); the declared value is the WORST of the eight and draw_spread carries the range, for mean_abs/within8_frac/ssim AND for interior_exact_frac, all_exact_frac and interior_frac. MEASURED THROUGH THE CHECK THAT GRADES IT, `check_visual_fidelity`, and one of the eight draws IS the draw the check takes -- it calls `sample_states(n)` with no rng, which is seed 0, the same fixed draw every time. The previous declaration was measured by a probe that averaged |diff| over the colour channels while `pixel_agreement` averages the per-pixel channel MAX, so it read 0.89/255 low and no widening rule could have covered the gap. The frame is a baked MuJoCo plate composited with MJWarp movers through the mover segmentation LUT, with gl_rounding and the shared out-of-range-spot correction applied. job 6433493 on gpu2109.oscar.ccv.brown.edu",
